## TL;DR

```bash
cd <repo-root>
bash tools/scratch/compose-domain/{{RUN_ID}}/graduate.sh
# follow the smoke instructions printed at the end
```

The script is **idempotent** — re-running is a no-op. If anything goes
wrong mid-run, it aborts loudly. Rollback at the end of this doc.

## What graduate.sh does

| # | Step | Affects |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Validate prereqs | (read-only) |
| 2 | Copy sandbox files | `verticals/{{VERTICAL_NAME}}/skills/`, `verticals/{{VERTICAL_NAME}}/personae/`, `verticals/{{VERTICAL_NAME}}/mcp_tools/`, `verticals/{{VERTICAL_NAME}}/entity_projections/` |
| 3 | Register Durable functions | `verticals/{{VERTICAL_NAME}}/durable.py` — appends orchestrator + activity triggers between sentinel markers |
| 4 | Register graph builders | `api/functions/graphs/__init__.py` — adds `build_*_workflow` exports |
| 5 | Register pack business declarations | `verticals/{{VERTICAL_NAME}}/spawners.py`, `verticals/{{VERTICAL_NAME}}/domains.py`, `verticals/{{VERTICAL_NAME}}/functions.py` — sentinel-guarded appends |
| 6 | Validate and print smoke commands | (read-only) |

Each patch step is idempotent: it checks for a unique anchor before
appending, so re-running graduate.sh is safe.

